From: Talos Linux <bugs@siderolabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boot: skip El Torito partition UUID discovery

systemd v261 added disk_get_part_uuid_eltorito(), which is reached from
disk_get_part_uuid() whenever the booted image's device path carries a CDROM
node instead of a GPT HARDDRIVE node -- i.e. on every El Torito CD/DVD boot.
It is called from export_common_variables() (so from both sd-boot and sd-stub)
and again directly from sd-stub for StubDevicePartUUID.

The new code touches the raw optical device in ways nothing did before: it
calls BS->ConnectController() on it recursively, then issues unaligned
sub-block EFI_DISK_IO_PROTOCOL reads probing for a GPT header at four
candidate sector sizes. Some firmware faults in that path and brings the
machine down with a synchronous exception before the kernel is entered.
Reported against UTM on arm64, where Talos v1.14.0-alpha.2 (systemd 260)
boots and v1.14.0-beta.0 (systemd 261) does not:

    https://github.com/siderolabs/talos/issues/14029

Drop the fallback and restore the systemd <= 260 behavior. The only
consequence is that LoaderDevicePartUUID/StubDevicePartUUID are left unset
when booting off a CD/DVD.

--- a/src/boot/part-discovery.c
+++ b/src/boot/part-discovery.c
@@ -321,6 +321,7 @@
         return EFI_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+__attribute__((unused))
 static char16_t* disk_get_part_uuid_eltorito(const EFI_DEVICE_PATH *dp) {
         EFI_STATUS err;
 
@@ -473,6 +474,17 @@
                 return xasprintf(GUID_FORMAT_STR, GUID_FORMAT_VAL(hd->SignatureGuid));
         }
 
-        /* No GPT partition node found — try El Torito device path as fallback */
-        return disk_get_part_uuid_eltorito(dp);
+        /* No GPT partition node found.
+         *
+         * Upstream falls back to disk_get_part_uuid_eltorito() here, which probes the underlying
+         * optical device via EFI_DISK_IO_PROTOCOL (sub-block reads at four candidate GPT sector
+         * sizes) and additionally calls ConnectController() on it recursively. Some firmware
+         * implementations fault in that path, taking the machine down with a synchronous exception
+         * before the kernel is ever entered:
+         *
+         *     https://github.com/siderolabs/talos/issues/14029
+         *
+         * The only thing lost by skipping this is Loader/StubDevicePartUUID being unset when
+         * booting off an El Torito CD/DVD, which is the behavior systemd <= 260 had. */
+        return NULL;
 }
